<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Daily Scrum - Monitoring</title><link href="https://blog.florijnconsultancy.nl/" rel="alternate"></link><link href="https://blog.florijnconsultancy.nl/feeds/monitoring.atom.xml" rel="self"></link><id>https://blog.florijnconsultancy.nl/</id><updated>2026-11-22T00:00:00+01:00</updated><subtitle>A personal blog</subtitle><entry><title>Hoe MyMonitor mijn netwerk bewaakt</title><link href="https://blog.florijnconsultancy.nl/articles/mymonitor-netwerkdiagram.html" rel="alternate"></link><published>2026-11-22T00:00:00+01:00</published><updated>2026-11-22T00:00:00+01:00</updated><author><name>Peter Florijn</name></author><id>tag:blog.florijnconsultancy.nl,2026-11-22:/articles/mymonitor-netwerkdiagram.html</id><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;Hoe MyMonitor vanaf een Mac lokale apparaten controleert en meldingen&amp;nbsp;verstuurt.&lt;/p&gt;</summary><content type="html">&lt;p&gt;MyMonitor draait op een Mac en brengt de bereikbaarheid van apparaten samen in een lokaal dashboard. Ik open het dashboard op de Mac zelf of vanaf een browser op hetzelfde&amp;nbsp;netwerk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/png;base64," class="uml" alt="uml diagram" title="" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Per apparaat kan MyMonitor een ping sturen, een &lt;span class="caps"&gt;TCP&lt;/span&gt;-poort controleren of een &lt;span class="caps"&gt;HTTP&lt;/span&gt;-verzoek doen. Voor Home Connect haalt het dashboard apparaatinformatie op via de externe &lt;span class="caps"&gt;API&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Een afzonderlijk script kan ook pingen als het dashboard gesloten is. Als ik e-mailmeldingen inschakel, stuurt dat script via &lt;span class="caps"&gt;SMTP&lt;/span&gt; een bericht zodra een apparaat uitvalt of weer bereikbaar&amp;nbsp;is.&lt;/p&gt;</content><category term="Monitoring"></category><category term="mymonitor"></category><category term="network"></category><category term="plantuml"></category></entry><entry><title>Helpdesk and wallboard</title><link href="https://blog.florijnconsultancy.nl/articles/helpdesk-and-wallboard.html" rel="alternate"></link><published>2013-05-12T11:55:00+02:00</published><updated>2013-05-12T11:55:00+02:00</updated><author><name>Peter Florijn</name></author><id>tag:blog.florijnconsultancy.nl,2013-05-12:/articles/helpdesk-and-wallboard.html</id><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;One of my projects involves the requirement to install a &lt;a href="http://www.atlassian.com/wallboards/"&gt;wallboard&lt;/a&gt; to show the &lt;span class="caps"&gt;ACD&lt;/span&gt; queue of our helpdesk and as a bonus we would like to show the scrumboard our development teams use. I&amp;rsquo;m looking into a Samsung &lt;span class="caps"&gt;LED&lt;/span&gt; monitor / Samsung Smart &lt;span class="caps"&gt;TV&lt;/span&gt; as part of the&amp;nbsp;solution.&lt;/p&gt;
</summary><content type="html">&lt;p&gt;One of my projects involves the requirement to install a &lt;a href="http://www.atlassian.com/wallboards/"&gt;wallboard&lt;/a&gt; to show the &lt;span class="caps"&gt;ACD&lt;/span&gt; queue of our helpdesk and as a bonus we would like to show the scrumboard our development teams use. I&amp;rsquo;m looking into a Samsung &lt;span class="caps"&gt;LED&lt;/span&gt; monitor / Samsung Smart &lt;span class="caps"&gt;TV&lt;/span&gt; as part of the&amp;nbsp;solution.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;p toc&gt;Contents&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="what-is-a-wallboard"&gt;What is a wallboard?&lt;a class="headerlink" href="#what-is-a-wallboard" title="Permanent link"&gt;&amp;para;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A wallboard is a type of information radiator that displays vital data about the progress of the development team. Similar to a scoreboard at a sporting event, wallboards are large, highly visible and easy to understand for anyone walking&amp;nbsp;by.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Traditional wallboards are made of paper or use sticky notes on a wall. Electronic wallboards are very effective since they update automatically with real-time data ensuring that people check back&amp;nbsp;regularly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="software-used-by-others"&gt;Software used by others&lt;a class="headerlink" href="#software-used-by-others" title="Permanent link"&gt;&amp;para;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
